        "id": 8435,
        "name": "trudge",
        "username": "trudge",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trudge/{size}/2062_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-07-30T04:17:31.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I was thinking about Miss Information, and had a couple thoughts.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>1) Miss Information seems to fill the niche of comedic Outside-of-Reality-Villain for this universe (kind of like Mr.<span> Mxyzptlk</span> or Ambush Bug, she doesn't quite belong in the usual comic reality).&nbsp; She's obsessed with the Freedom Four, and her powers seem to involve a lot of reality manipulation, and her goal is largely to screw with the Freedom Four in comedic ways.&nbsp; Second, she seems to come from a sort of parallel universe or timeline, so it's like she isn't *supposed* to be in the main timeline's reality.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>2) I think she has some sort of meta power that activates when she's defeated - it's a sort of defensive retcon.&nbsp; She gets defeated, but no one remembers that she went rogue (including Aminia).&nbsp; Instead, Aminia becomes the sweet assistant again, and no one really remembers that she was a reality bending supervillain.&nbsp; Then, sometime later, the Miss Information rises again with a new plan to betray the heroes.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Not sure if I'm grasping at straws though.&nbsp; Though, if her narrative niche is to be the outside-of-reality villain, it would affect what her nemesis should look like.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:38:57.667Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
