        "raw": "<p>I was thinking about Miss Information, and had a couple thoughts.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>1) Miss Information seems to fill the niche of comedic Outside-of-Reality-Villain for this universe (kind of like Mr.<span dir=\"auto\"> Mxyzptlk</span> or Ambush Bug, she doesn&#39;t quite belong in the usual comic reality).&nbsp; She&#39;s obsessed with the Freedom Four, and her powers seem to involve a lot of reality manipulation, and her goal is largely to screw with the Freedom Four in comedic ways.&nbsp; Second, she seems to come from a sort of parallel universe or timeline, so it&#39;s like she isn&#39;t *supposed* to be in the main timeline&#39;s reality.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>2) I think she has some sort of meta power that activates when she&#39;s defeated - it&#39;s a sort of defensive retcon.&nbsp; She gets defeated, but no one remembers that she went rogue (including Aminia).&nbsp; Instead, Aminia becomes the sweet assistant again, and no one really remembers that she was a reality bending supervillain.&nbsp; Then, sometime later, the Miss Information rises again with a new plan to betray the heroes.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Not sure if I&#39;m grasping at straws though.&nbsp; Though, if her narrative niche is to be the outside-of-reality villain, it would affect what her nemesis should look like.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
